  "qa": [
    "The 60px-high closed-mouth patch covers the entire old smile including both corners, and leaves nose/chin outside. Its conservative clip is narrower at lower cheek corners to keep source jaw edges out even with fixed registration offsets.",
    "Do not replace approved openSmall/openWide patches or mouthReference. These crop proposals apply only to the four new closed-mouth expression states.",
    "Review actual compositions at zero gaze, close-up and with eyes blinking; source per-pixel skin shades may differ and need boundary QA.",
    "Earlier left-shiftRight drawings had a neutral-looking seam or incorrect center direction; earlier right-shiftRight had a tooth wedge. Final sources were remeasured after replacement. Left native seam center458 is viewer-left of neutral461.5; right center655 is viewer-left of neutral660.5. No horizontal registration is used for any directional state.",
    "Directional anchors retain real native source lateral displacement; never register both shift sources back to neutral mouthReference.x.",
    "Final left shiftRight corner has a slightly stronger closed crease than the other three shifts. Its material is uniformly dark, without a tooth-white patch; verify final 3x composition for stylistic balance. Do not equate metadata/native bounds tests with user visual acceptance."
  ],
